# Claude Code notes

`AGENTS.md` (imported above) is the team rulebook and wins on any conflict. This file adds only how
Claude Code uses its tools here. Engine path and personal permissions go in `CLAUDE.local.md`
(gitignored).

## Pick the narrowest tool

| Need | Use |
|---|---|
| Editor state: actors, assets, levels, widgets, materials, DataTables, PIE | Unreal MCP. First call of a session: `list_toolsets`. Keep `docs/MCP_TOOLS.md` current |
| Five or more similar edits, imports, level layout | A script in `scripts/editor/`, run through MCP Python or `ue.py python` |
| Build, package, tests | The `unreal-engine` skill's `ue.py`, run in the background; read the log when it exits |
| Look at the editor or game | MCP viewport capture, or `capture_window.ps1`; then read the PNG |
| Feel, sound, taste | Ask the human for a specific check |

## MCP etiquette

- One mutation at a time, read before write, check every result for success.
- After an editor restart the connection drops: confirm the port listens, then reconnect with `/mcp`.
- Hand non-editor work (data, docs, generator scripts, reviews) to subagents. MCP stays in the main
  session.
